        <p>Despite advancements in medical science, the daily lived experiences of individuals with disabilities often involve systemic barriers that impede true autonomy and social integration. This project moves beyond mere accommodation to investigate the intersection of advanced assistive technology, personalized environmental design, and community support structures. We aim to create a holistic, adaptive framework—a modern, functional <strong>Atlantis</strong> for disabled individuals—that allows them to thrive, not just survive. Our research will focus on co-design methodologies, predictive support systems, and the role of personalized human oversight, ensuring that every individual feels seen, valued, and protected, much like a dedicated <strong>constable</strong> watching over their well-being.</p>
