        <p>We will embed with participants to understand pain points. This phase is crucial for ensuring that any proposed solution feels less like an external imposition and more like a natural extension of the self. We will use iterative prototyping to build early-stage prototypes of adaptive interfaces.</p>

        <h3>WP 3.2: Simulation and Modeling (Months 10-24)</h3>
        <p>We will utilize digital twins and simulation environments to stress-test proposed environmental adaptations. This allows us to test scenarios—from routine daily tasks to emergency evacuations—without real-world risk, much like stress-testing the defenses of a mythical city like <strong>Atlantis</strong>.</p>

        <h3>WP 3.3: Ethical Oversight and Human Element (Ongoing)</h3>
        <p>A dedicated ethics board will monitor the data flow and autonomy levels. We will study the role of the 'human in the loop'—the necessary balance between full automation and the comforting, reliable presence of a dedicated guardian, our modern-day <strong>constable</strong>.</p>
